- sha: 0a37242
  date: 2026-10-12
  kind: fix
  files:
    - ui/src/domain/presets.ts
    - ui/src/domain/presets.test.ts
  notes: |
    ROOT CAUSE for remaining silent presets (retro-lead, lush-pad,
    analog-bass, 808-king, toms-funk, etc):

    Strudel transpiler wraps every sound name in mini() (mini-notation
    parser). mini() treats ':' as a control-modifier separator,
    splitting "name:n" into [{ s: 'name', n: 'n' }]. So all presets
    using bank:sound syntax got split:
        s("synth:lead-e4")  →  s="synth", n="lead-e4"
        s("drums:bd*4")     →  s="drums", n="bd*4"

    superdough destructured value.s and did getSound(s) — neither
    "synth" nor "drums" is registered as a sound, so each lookup
    threw "sound <name> not found! Is it loaded?".

    FIX: rewrite presets to use s("bank_sound") syntax. strudel.json
    manifests already use bank_sound convention. mini() does NOT
    split on '_' (only on ':'), so the sound name is preserved as
    one atom.

    Verified empirically:
      s("synth:lead-e4").firstCycle() → [{ s: "synth:lead-e4" }]  (raw)
      s(m('synth:lead-e4', 0)).firstCycle()
        → [{ s: "synth", n: "lead-e4" }]   ← what transpiled code produces
      s("synth_lead-e4").firstCycle() → [{ s: "synth_lead-e4" }]  ✓
      s(m('synth_lead-e4', 0)).firstCycle()
        → [{ s: "synth_lead-e4" }]         ✓ (correct)

    19 sound-name occurrences rewritten across 7 presets. Tests
    updated to match bank_ format. Full suite 255/255 pass.
    typecheck clean. vite build OK. bin/deploy.sh deployed to
    /var/lib/wavecode/dist. Verified retro-lead now loads
    synth_lead-e4 / synth_bass-c2 / synth_lead-g4 from the sampler
    ("sound synth not found" error gone).
- sha: 5ea8847
  date: 2026-10-12
  kind: fix
  files:
    - ui/src/domain/presets.ts
  notes: |
    IDM-glitch preset was using .bitcrush(), which doesn't exist
    in Strudel (no such effect). At eval time, the throw:
        TypeError: s(...).bitcrush is not a function
    killed the entire stack — no sounds played.

    FIX: replaced .bitcrush(4, 8000) with .crush(4, 8000). Strudel's
    .crush(bits, rate) defaults to 4-bit reduction and 8000 Hz
    sample rate — same character the IDM-glitch was going for
    (bit-reduced noise percussion layer).

    Verified empirically via browser: IDM-glitch now plays the
    bd / sd / hh layers (after the bank_sound fix) plus the
    bit-crushed white noise percussion. lastEvalErr=null,
    samples load (4 in test).

    Reference: superdough/dist/index.mjs:671
      crush: { node: "crush-processor", param: "crush" }
    Bitcrush would correspond to crush with extra parameters, but
    Strudel doesn't expose .bitcrush as a separate control.
- sha: a140d7c
  date: 2026-10-12
  kind: fix
  files:
    - ui/src/infrastructure/audio/SampleLoader.ts
    - ui/src/infrastructure/audio/SampleLoader.test.ts
    - ui/src/infrastructure/audio/strudel.d.ts
    - ui/src/infrastructure/audio/strudelPatches.ts
    - ui/src/infrastructure/audio/strudelPatches.test.ts
    - math/wavecode-sample-bank-underscore/witness
  notes: |
    FOURTH hidden bug in the same surface: the very first haps of a
    preset were silently dropped because superdough's sampler
    races the audio scheduler against fetch+decodeAudioData.

    superdough/dist/index.mjs:989:
      if (u.currentTime > e) {
        j('loading took too long', 'highlight');
        Y(y);
        return;  // hap dropped silently
      }

    fetch().arrayBuffer().decodeAudioData() takes 80–160 ms (logged
    as "done! loaded 5.2 KiB in 89ms" for bd.mp3). When the scheduler
    fires the very first hap of `s("bd sd hh bd sd hh")`, the audio
    context clock has already advanced past the scheduled start, so
    the hap is dropped. User sees `lastEvalErr=null` but hears the
    2nd/3rd haps instead of the 1st, with `[sampler] loading sound
    'bd:0' took too long` once per cycle until the cache warms.

    FIX: after `samples()` resolves each bank, eagerly call
    `loadBuffer(url, audioContext, label)` for every URL in every
    sample bank. This populates superdough's internal `tt[url]`
    promise cache so the very first haps hit warm cache instead of
    fetching fresh.

    Fire-and-forget: `void Promise.allSettled(promises)` so the
    preload does not block the registration promise. If the user
    clicks Play before preloads finish, only the very first cycle
    is at risk (which has 4+ cycles of lead time before the audio
    context unlocks via `LiveAudioEngine.unlockAudioContext()`).

    ARCHITECTURAL: this commit also retires the previous
    `applyBankAliasFallback` / `DEFAULT_BANK_FALLBACKS` machinery
    from strudelPatches.ts. That helper registered bare bank-name
    aliases (`drums` → `drums_bd`) as a post-load patch, but the
    same job is done more cleanly by `addBareAliases()` inside
    SampleLoader.ts (which iterates ALL bank_sound keys and
    publishes bare `sound` aliases — covers more cases than the
    hard-coded fallback map ever did, and unifies registration
    with sample loading in one place).

    After this commit strudelPatches.ts is reduced to its two
    surviving helpers: `wrapStrudelLogger` (logger.mjs CSS strip)
    and `applyVoicingAliases` (tonal/voicings.mjs chord-symbol
    aliases). The third slot is gone.

    Verified empirically:
    - SampleLoader.test.ts: loadBufferMock is called once per
      sample URL in every registered bank (14 drums samples
      verified; piano + synth symmetric).
    - vitest: 275/275 pass (was 280/280 before; 5 fewer because
      retired applyBankAliasFallback tests dropped).
    - typecheck: clean.
    - vite build: OK (PWA precache 19 entries, 1422 KiB).

    OUTSTANDING (NOT in this commit):
    - AudioWorkletNode intermittent error after rapid eval cycles.
      Pre-existing in Strudel 1.3 — worklet processor is released
      after some idle period. Not blocking sample playback.
      Sample-only presets (jazz, toms-funk, retro-lead) play
      correctly.
    - strudelPatches.ts carries an updated docstring noting the
      retirement of patch #3 (`applyBankAliasFallback`) so future
      readers don't try to reintroduce it.

    Refs: superdough/dist/index.mjs:989 (`currentTime > e` early
    return); superdough/dist/index.mjs:1003-1020 (loadBuffer
    populates the `tt[url]` cache).